.TH RATTPKG 1 "2026-10-05" "Rattpack 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
rattpkg \- resolve, fetch, and verify Rattpack package dependencies
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B rattpkg resolve
.RB [ \--update ]
.RB [ \--allow-floating ]
.RB [ \-C " DIRECTORY" ]
.br
.B rattpkg fetch
.RB [ \-C " DIRECTORY" ]
.br
.B rattpkg verify
.RB [ \-C " DIRECTORY" ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B rattpkg
reads the Rattscript Rattpkg manifest, resolves dependencies, and maintains a
TOML lockfile and a content-addressed source cache. Exactly one command is
required; there is no default operation or positional package selection.
.PP
Dependencies may come from a registry, HTTP(S), FTP, or Git. HTTP and FTP
archives require a SHA-256 checksum. Git dependencies use a tag or revision;
floating branches require explicit permission. A Git remote need not contain
a Rattpkg: a package can be synthesized from its Rattspec or treated as raw
sources. Supported archives are tar, tar.gz, tar.xz, and zip; traversal and
archive link entries are rejected.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B resolve
Read Rattpkg, obtain required content, and write Rattpkg.lock. A matching
manifest fingerprint reuses an existing lockfile unless \--update is given;
its pinned content is fetched and verified. Prints "resolved Rattpkg.lock".
.TP
.B fetch
Read Rattpkg.lock, fill missing cache entries, and check existing entries.
Does not choose newer versions or update the lockfile.
Prints "packages fetched".
.TP
.B verify
Re-hash all locked package trees. Does not download missing trees or repair
changed ones. Prints "packages verified".
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-C " DIRECTORY" ", \--directory=" DIRECTORY
Select the directory containing Rattpkg and Rattpkg.lock.
Default: current directory.
.TP
.B \--update
Resolve fresh selections rather than reusing a matching lockfile.
Applies to resolve.
.TP
.B \--allow-floating
Permit Git branch references when resolving new selections.
.TP
.B \-h, \--help
Display help and exit.
.TP
.B \--version
Display the version and exit.
.PP
Boolean long options accept negative spellings such as \--no-update.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I Rattpkg
Rattscript package manifest declaring package identity and dependencies.
.TP
.I Rattpkg.lock
TOML lockfile containing immutable dependency selections. Commit it for
applications; do not commit it for libraries.
.TP
.I $XDG_CACHE_HOME/rattpack/pkgs/NAME/HASH/
Verified package source trees. On POSIX, XDG_CACHE_HOME defaults to ~/.cache.
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/rattpack/Config.toml
Configuration, including pkg.registry and pkg.mirrors. On POSIX,
XDG_CONFIG_HOME defaults to ~/.config. Config.yaml is an alternative;
TOML wins with W_DUAL_CONFIG if both exist.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Configuration base directory. Windows uses APPDATA instead.
.TP
.B XDG_CACHE_HOME
Package cache base directory on POSIX.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 indicates success, help, or version output; 1 indicates an application
diagnostic, resolution, download, or verification failure; 2 indicates argument
parsing failure. Diagnostics go to standard error.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
rattpkg resolve
rattpkg resolve \--update \-C workspace
rattpkg resolve \--allow-floating
rattpkg fetch
rattpkg verify
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR rattbuild (1),
.BR rattsc (1),
.BR rattspec (1)
.PP
The installed Rattpack manual describes manifests, registries, and lockfiles.
